# Security Rules

- Never commit secrets, tokens, or private keys. Use environment variables only.
- `Settings` uses `extra="forbid"` — only declared fields may appear in `.env`.
- `SECRET_KEY` must be >= 32 characters in production; not the development default.
- Production `CORS_ORIGINS` must use HTTPS and no localhost/127.0.0.1 origins.
- Production `DATABASE_URL` must be PostgreSQL; SQLite is rejected in production.
- JWT expiry is configurable via `jwt_expiry_minutes`; do not hardcode.
- `/metrics` requires bearer token authentication.
- `current_claims` reads tenant identity only from the verified access token.
- TypeSafe integration is optional and degrades gracefully when disabled/unavailable.
